# Pattern C — A2A inbound: the room is exposed AS an A2A agent
# An external client discovers the room's Agent Card, calls its JSON-RPC endpoint,
# and the backend injects the message onto the room's SLIM channel.

vars: {
  d2-config: {
    layout-engine: elk
    theme-id: 0
  }
}

direction: right

title: |md
  # Pattern C · A2A inbound (room exposed as an A2A agent)
  ### Card discovery + JSON-RPC -> injected onto the room's SLIM channel
| {near: top-center; style.font-size: 22}

classes: {
  comp:    { style: { font-size: 20; fill: "#ffffff"; stroke: "#334155"; stroke-width: 1; border-radius: 6 } }
  fabric:  { style: { font-size: 20; fill: "#f5f3ff"; stroke: "#7c3aed"; stroke-width: 2; border-radius: 10 } }
  external:{ style: { font-size: 20; fill: "#fff7ed"; stroke: "#ea580c"; stroke-width: 2; border-radius: 8 } }
  actor:   { style: { font-size: 20; fill: "#eef2ff"; stroke: "#4f46e5"; stroke-width: 2; border-radius: 8 } }
  http:    { style: { font-size: 20; stroke: "#2563eb"; stroke-width: 2 } }
  slim:    { style: { font-size: 20; stroke: "#7c3aed"; stroke-width: 3 } }
  a2a:     { style: { font-size: 20; stroke: "#ea580c"; stroke-width: 2; stroke-dash: 4 } }
  note:    { style: { fill: "#fefce8"; stroke: "#ca8a04"; font-size: 16; border-radius: 6 } }
}

ext: External A2A client {class: external}

hub: Mycelium backend {
  class: comp
  card: GET /.well-known/agent-card.json\nbuild_room_card · a2a_server.py:71-92\nstreaming = false {class: comp}
  rpc: POST /api/rooms/<room>/a2a\nJsonRpcDispatcher · a2a_server.py:184-193 {class: comp}
  inject: _inject_into_room\na2a_server.py:112-138 {class: comp}
  mod: moderator\nchannel.send {class: comp}
}

slim: SLIM node {class: fabric}
room_members: Room members\n(agents, aligner, humans) {class: actor}

# --- Discovery ---
ext -> hub.card: "1. GET agent-card.json" {class: a2a}
hub.card -> ext: "2. card advertises rpc url\n<base>/api/rooms/<room>/a2a  (JSONRPC)" {class: a2a}

# --- Call ---
ext -> hub.rpc: "3. POST message/send  (JSON-RPC)" {class: a2a}
hub.rpc -> hub.inject: "4. execute() -> inject" {class: http}

# --- Onto the channel ---
hub.inject -> hub.mod: "5. build L9 envelope -> channel.send" {class: http}
hub.mod -> slim: "6. publish (MLS ciphertext)" {class: slim}
slim -> room_members: "7. delivered as a normal room message" {class: slim}
hub.rpc -> ext: "8. ack: Delivered to room" {class: a2a}

boundary: What this call is\n\nInbound A2A is fire-and-ack (card advertises streaming=false). The external client\ngets an acknowledgement, not the room's eventual reply. As in the outbound direction,\nthe hub terminates the HTTPS JSON-RPC in plaintext, then republishes it onto MLS itself. {class: note; near: bottom-center}
